# Instruction:
Write Swift code to develop an iOS App called “Tennis Score Tracker” to track tennis scores for a complete match up to three sets. Allow user to input scores on the App. Enable advanced option for user to track details of every point such as whether it was a winner, unforced error, forced error, ace, return winner or serve winner.  
# Output (a):
Below is one example of how you might build an iOS “Tennis Score Tracker” app using SwiftUI. In this example the code defines data models for a match, set scores and individual point details (with advanced point–by–point tracking), and provides a simple UI that lets the user update scores for up to three sets as well as toggle an “Advanced Mode” so the user can record extra details (winner, error type, ace, etc.) for each point. (In a production app you would likely expand error handling, persistence, and view navigation further.) 

You can paste this code into a new SwiftUI project in Xcode. (Each file can be split appropriately in a real project; here everything is shown in one file for brevity.)

--------------------------------------------------------------
import SwiftUI

// MARK: – Data Models

// Enum to represent point details available in advanced mode.
enum PointType: String, CaseIterable, Identifiable {
    var id: String { self.rawValue }

    case winner = "Winner"
    case unforcedError = "Unforced Error"
    case forcedError = "Forced Error"
    case ace = "Ace"
    case returnWinner = "Return Winner"
    case serveWinner = "Serve Winner"
}

// This struct tracks an individual point’s details.
struct TennisPoint: Identifiable {
    let id = UUID()
    let timestamp: Date = Date()
    var scoredBy: String  // e.g., "Player 1" or "Player 2"
    var detail: PointType?
}

// This struct represents a single set’s score.
struct SetScore: Identifiable {
    let id = UUID()
    var gamesPlayer1: Int = 0
    var gamesPlayer2: Int = 0
}

// This ObservableObject represents the overall tennis match.
class TennisMatch: ObservableObject {
    @Published var sets: [SetScore] = [SetScore(), SetScore(), SetScore()]  // up to three sets
    // An array that holds details of every point when advanced mode is enabled.
    @Published var detailedPoints: [TennisPoint] = []

    // Which set is currently active (0, 1, or 2)
    @Published var currentSet: Int = 0

    // Optionally track if the match is in advanced mode.
    @Published var advancedMode: Bool = false

    // Methods to update the score.
    func addGame(forPlayer player: Int) {
        // Check that current set index is within bounds.
        guard currentSet < sets.count else { return }
        if player == 1 {
            sets[currentSet].gamesPlayer1 += 1
        } else {
            sets[currentSet].gamesPlayer2 += 1
        }
        // Optionally, you may add logic for finishing a set before continuing.
    }

    // Record a point with an optional advanced detail.
    func recordPoint(scoredBy: String, detail: PointType? = nil) {
        let point = TennisPoint(scoredBy: scoredBy, detail: detail)
        detailedPoints.append(point)
    }

    // Reset the match (optional helper)
    func resetMatch() {
        sets = [SetScore(), SetScore(), SetScore()]
        detailedPoints = []
        currentSet = 0
    }
}

// MARK: – Views

// Main ContentView that shows score updates and advanced options.
struct ContentView: View {
    @ObservedObject var match = TennisMatch()

    // State for controlling a sheet for advanced details.
    @State private var showingAdvancedSheet = false
    // Temporary state for storing advanced point selection.
    @State private var selectedPointType: PointType = .winner

    var body: some View {
        NavigationView {
            VStack(alignment: .leading, spacing: 20) {
                Text("Tennis Score Tracker")
                    .font(.largeTitle)
                    .bold()

                Group {
                    // Display current set scores
                    Text("Current Set: \(match.currentSet + 1)")
                        .font(.headline)
                    HStack {
                        VStack {
                            Text("Player 1")
                                .bold()
                            Text("Games: \(match.sets[match.currentSet].gamesPlayer1)")
                        }
                        Spacer()
                        VStack {
                            Text("Player 2")
                                .bold()
                            Text("Games: \(match.sets[match.currentSet].gamesPlayer2)")
                        }
                    }
                }
                .padding()
                .background(Color(UIColor.secondarySystemBackground))
                .cornerRadius(10)

                // Buttons to add a game to each player.
                HStack {
                    Button("Add Game to Player 1") {
                        match.addGame(forPlayer: 1)
                        recordSimplePoint(scoredBy: "Player 1")
                    }
                    .buttonStyle(PrimaryButtonStyle())

                    Button("Add Game to Player 2") {
                        match.addGame(forPlayer: 2)
                        recordSimplePoint(scoredBy: "Player 2")
                    }
                    .buttonStyle(PrimaryButtonStyle())
                }

                // Advanced mode toggle.
                Toggle("Advanced Mode", isOn: $match.advancedMode)
                    .padding([.leading, .trailing])

                // When in advanced mode, allow logging details for a point.
                if match.advancedMode {
                    VStack(alignment: .leading) {
                        Text("Record Detailed Point:")
                            .bold()
                        HStack {
                            // Selecting which player scored.
                            Button("Player 1") {
                                showingAdvancedSheet = true
                            }
                            .buttonStyle(SecondaryButtonStyle())

                            Button("Player 2") {
                                showingAdvancedSheet = true
                            }
                            .buttonStyle(SecondaryButtonStyle())
                        }
                        Text("Tip: Your advanced detail will be attached when you choose the point type in the next dialog.")
                            .font(.footnote)
                            .foregroundColor(.gray)
                    }
                    .padding()
                }

                // List out detailed points (if any)
                if !match.detailedPoints.isEmpty {
                    Text("Detailed Points Log:")
                        .font(.headline)
                    List(match.detailedPoints) { point in
                        VStack(alignment: .leading) {
                            Text("\(point.scoredBy) scored @ \(point.timestamp.formatted(date: .omitted, time: .shortened))")
                            if let detail = point.detail {
                                Text("Detail: \(detail.rawValue)").font(.subheadline).foregroundColor(.gray)
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    .frame(height: 200)
                }

                Spacer()
            }
            .padding()
            .navigationTitle("Tennis Score Tracker")
            .sheet(isPresented: $showingAdvancedSheet, content: {
                AdvancedPointDetailView(match: match, isPresented: $showingAdvancedSheet)
            })
        }
    }

    // Helper function to record a point with basic info.
    func recordSimplePoint(scoredBy: String) {
        // When advanced mode is off, record the point with no additional data.
        if !match.advancedMode {
            match.recordPoint(scoredBy: scoredBy, detail: nil)
        }
    }
}

// A separate view to select the advanced point detail.
// In this example, once a user selects a point type, the point is recorded.
struct AdvancedPointDetailView: View {
    @ObservedObject var match: TennisMatch
    @Binding var isPresented: Bool

    // For simplicity, we'll ask which point type to record.
    @State private var selectedPlayer: String = ""

    var body: some View {
        NavigationView {
            Form {
                Section(header: Text("Select Player")) {
                    // Buttons for player selection.
                    Button("Player 1") {
                        selectedPlayer = "Player 1"
                    }
                    Button("Player 2") {
                        selectedPlayer = "Player 2"
                    }
                }

                Section(header: Text("Select Point Detail Type")) {
                    ForEach(PointType.allCases) { type in
                        Button(action: {
                            if selectedPlayer.isEmpty {
                                // If a player wasn’t chosen yet, default to Player 1.
                                selectedPlayer = "Player 1"
                            }
                            // Record the advanced point.
                            match.recordPoint(scoredBy: selectedPlayer, detail: type)
                            isPresented = false
                        }) {
                            Text(type.rawValue)
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
            .navigationTitle("Advanced Point Entry")
            .navigationBarItems(trailing: Button("Cancel") {
                isPresented = false
            })
        }
    }
}

// MARK: – Button Styles (for better UI)
struct PrimaryButtonStyle: ButtonStyle {
    func makeBody(configuration: Configuration) -> some View {
        configuration.label
            .padding()
            .background(Color.blue.opacity(configuration.isPressed ? 0.7 : 1.0))
            .foregroundColor(.white)
            .cornerRadius(8)
    }
}
struct SecondaryButtonStyle: ButtonStyle {
    func makeBody(configuration: Configuration) -> some View {
        configuration.label
            .padding(8)
            .background(Color.gray.opacity(configuration.isPressed ? 0.5 : 0.3))
            .foregroundColor(.black)
            .cornerRadius(8)
    }
}

// MARK: – App Entry Point
@main
struct TennisScoreTrackerApp: App {
    var body: some Scene {
        WindowGroup {
            ContentView()
        }
    }
}

--------------------------------------------------------------

Explanation:

1. The data models (PointType, TennisPoint, SetScore, TennisMatch) encapsulate the application’s data. TennisMatch is an ObservableObject so changes in scores and detailed points immediately update the UI.

2. The ContentView shows the current set (with game scores for each player) along with buttons to add a game (which simultaneously records a point in basic mode). A Toggle allows the user to switch on “Advanced Mode” so that a sheet (AdvancedPointDetailView) appears letting the user choose which player scored and what type of point it was.

3. AdvancedPointDetailView uses a Form to capture the extra point detail and then calls match.recordPoint(scoredBy:detail:) to log that point.

Feel free to expand on this code to add more features (for example, handling actual tennis game scoring, set completion rules, persistence, or a more sophisticated UI). 
